From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read the held key under the lock of its client

CCECClient::CheckKeypressTimeout(), which the processor thread calls on
every pass of its loop, read m_iCurrentButton before taking the client's
lock, to return at once when no key is held. The threads that add keys
write it under that lock, and so does ResetKeypressState(), which
CLibCEC::Close() reaches through OnUnregister() while the processor
thread still runs (a data race). The check is now made under the lock.
The processor thread already takes this lock for every key it receives
and while a key is held, and no holder of the lock waits for the
processor thread, so the order of the locks does not change. What is
decided does not change.

Tests (outside the tree): libCEC built on the host with ThreadSanitizer,
with a thread that polls for key timeouts as the processor thread does
while another unregisters the client (a data race on m_iCurrentButton
before, none after), and with a Pulse-Eight adapter emulated on a pseudo
terminal, opened and closed many times.
---
 src/libcec/CECClient.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp b/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp
index 98f3748..69d357e 100644
--- a/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp
@@ -1300,10 +1300,13 @@ uint16_t CCECClient::CheckKeypressTimeout(void)
   key.keycode = CEC_USER_CONTROL_CODE_UNKNOWN;
   key.duration = 0;
 
-  if (m_iCurrentButton == CEC_USER_CONTROL_CODE_UNKNOWN)
-	  return (uint16_t)timeout;
   {
+    // m_iCurrentButton is written under this lock, by the threads that add keys and by
+    // ResetKeypressState() when the client is unregistered: read it under the lock too
     CLockObject lock(m_mutex);
+    if (m_iCurrentButton == CEC_USER_CONTROL_CODE_UNKNOWN)
+      return (uint16_t)timeout;
+
     uint64_t iNow = GetTimeMs();
     LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_DEBUG, "%s T:%.3f", __FUNCTION__, iNow*1e-3);
     cec_user_control_code comboKey(m_configuration.comboKey);
